## 2.  Triaged Scanner False Positives (Third-Party Noise)

The initial automated sweep flagged 11 instances of **CORS Wildcard/Arbitrary Origin with Credentials** as CRITICAL.

> **Analysis Verdict: FALSE POSITIVE (OUT OF SCOPE)**
> 
> **Endpoint:** `https://adservice.google.com/getconfig/pubvendors`
> - **Ownership:** Belongs to Google Advertising, not the inspected APK targets.
> - **Mechanism:** The endpoint returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://evil.com` on OPTIONS preflight, but on actual **GET**, it returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` without `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.
> - **Impact:** Browsers strictly refuse to include session cookies or credentials with wildcard `*`. No cross-origin user data theft is possible.

## 3.  Hardening & SDK Default Gaps

### A. Exported Firebase Activities (`GenericIdpActivity`, `RecaptchaActivity`)
- **Occurrences:** Found across MikuNime and ManhwaID targets.
- **Analysis:** These components are bundled by the standard Firebase Auth SDK (`com.google.firebase:firebase-auth`). While they are marked `android:exported="true"` to receive browser OAuth/reCAPTCHA intent callbacks, invoking them directly without valid cryptographic intent tokens yields an unhandled internal exception rather than privilege escalation.

### B. Application Data Backup (`android:allowBackup="true"`)
- **Analysis:** Allows extraction of private SharedPreferences and SQLite databases via `adb backup` if physical device access is obtained. Should be set to `android:allowBackup="false"` in release builds.

